nodecode-parallel-search is a rewrite of parallel-web's parallel-web/search-mcp:

  https://github.com/parallel-web/search-mcp
  commit 12f721b2b7ad29e63315884c008b5d77c2a4d7e4
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Parallel Web Systems (LICENSE)

The rewritten part is the package's whole point: two model-facing tools, web_search
and web_fetch, served by Parallel's hosted Streamable-HTTP MCP server at
https://search.parallel.ai/mcp. The original carries no code of its own -- one
plugin manifest, one mcp.json naming that server, and a skill teaching when to use
it -- so the rewrite is the client the original left to the harness: a JSON-RPC
client in Common Lisp over the image's own HTTP call, an initialize that claims the
session the server offers, the initialized note, and tools/call, reading an answer
whether it arrives as JSON or as an event stream. The two tools keep the same
names, the same arguments (objective, search_queries, max_results,
max_chars_per_result, urls) and the same answers: the server's own text, its
excerpts and its urls, unedited. The skill's guidance is kept as the primer
(help :parallel) prints and as the tool descriptions: search first, answer from
the excerpts, batch a broad task's queries into one call, fetch a page only when
it is needed, cite the urls, and expect the free tier to be rate limited. The
anonymous endpoint stays anonymous: no key, no environment variable, no header
the pasted config did not ask for.

What was left out is what belonged to the harness the package was written for:
the Agent Plugins manifest and the client manifests for each host (a Nodecode cell
declares its section, its tools and its manual topic in one form), the bundled
skill file as a file (the same words are the primer), the per-client install
instructions, and the MCP transport library the host provided. Nothing is
downloaded at run time and no code of the original runs here. The endpoint and
its free tier are the original's; the section beside them adds only a result
count, a timeout, and the address, for a user who points the cell at their own
MCP server.
